Station T-18 (Survey Area T) consists of a four-layer sequence. The profile begins with a low-resistivity top layer (15.7 $\Omega\cdot$m, 1.56 m), followed by a thick, high-resistivity layer (188.9 $\Omega\cdot$m, 15.69 m). The sequence continues with a slight decrease in resistivity for the third layer (183.8 $\Omega\cdot$m, 0.79 m) and a further decrease in the fourth layer (106.9 $\Omega\cdot$m).

Please note that the current on-file classification of "A-type" is incorrect. Based on the interpreted resistivity values ($15.7 < 188.9 > 183.8$ and $188.9 > 183.8 > 106.9$), the correct curve notation for this station is KQ.

