Station T-19 (Survey Area T) presents a resistivity profile characterized by a significant increase in the upper layers. The sequence begins with Layer 1 at 609.2 ohm-m, rising sharply to 7309.9 ohm-m in Layer 2, then decreasing to 4367.7 ohm-m in Layer 3, and finally rising slightly to 4556.7 ohm-m in Layer 4. 

Applying the curve-type notation rules, the first group (layers 1-2-3) follows a K-type pattern (increase then decrease), and the second group (layers 2-3-4) follows an H-type pattern (decrease then increase). Therefore, the calculated curve type is KH. Please note that the existing file classification of KQ-type is inconsistent with the interpreted layer model and should be updated.

